---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const trail = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }];
---
<Page
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What data Going Eagle collects, what it does not collect, and how the tools on this site handle the information you enter."
  intro="The short version: our tools run entirely in your browser and we do not store what you type into them."
  trail={trail}
>
  <h2>The calculators</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool on this site — the ball flight diagnostic, the handicap calculator and the rest —
    runs as JavaScript in your own browser. Scores, ratings and answers you enter are never
    transmitted to us, never written to a database, and disappear when you close the tab.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We may use privacy-respecting analytics to understand which pages are useful. When analytics
    are enabled, this page will name the provider and describe exactly what is collected. We will
    not add tracking without updating this page first.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    When you click an affiliate link, the destination retailer may set a cookie so they can
    attribute a purchase to us. That cookie is set by them, under their privacy policy, not ours.
    Our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> explains the arrangement.
  </p>

  <h2>Your browser storage</h2>
  <p>
    We store one thing locally: your light or dark theme preference. It stays in your browser,
    is never sent to us, and clearing your site data removes it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about any of this go through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
